      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a draft memo that's sure to please:\n\nSubject: Ergonomic Reminders for Remote Workers\n\nDear Team,\n\nAs we continue to work together to drive innovation and success, I want to take a moment to remind everyone about the importance of maintaining a comfortable and ergonomic workspace, even when working from home. Just like a well-organized and efficient team, a well-set-up workspace is crucial for productivity and overall well-being.\n\nWhen setting up your home office, remember to prioritize your physical comfort. Take a cue from the expert \"ergonomists\" of the forest, who have spent centuries perfecting the art of nest-building. Just as a sturdy nest requires a solid foundation, a comfortable workspace demands a well-arranged desk and chair.\n\nHere are some simple tips to get you started:\n\n* Position your monitor directly in front of you, at a distance of about 20-25 inches, and at a height that allows you to gaze slightly downward.\n* Keep your keyboard and mouse close to your body, with your wrists straight and your elbows at a 90-degree angle.\n* Adjust your chair height to ensure your feet are flat on the floor or on a footrest, with your knees at or below hip level.\n* Consider using",
